  "section": {
    "letter": "C",
    "heading": "Gdzie ona jest?",
    "meaning": {
      "en": "Where is she?"
    },
    "strands": [
      "G"
    ]
  },
  "tips": [
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l02-c-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l02-c-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "Być: where are you?"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "*Być* is irregular, and you met it in Starter: *jestem*, *jesteś*, *jest*, *jesteśmy*, *jesteście*, *są*. *Gdzie jesteś?* asks a friend where they are, and *jestem tutaj* answers \"I am here\". *Pan* and *pani* take *jest*: *gdzie pani jest?*"
      },
      "conjugation": {
        "verb": "być",
        "meaning": {
          "en": "to be"
        },
        "forms": {
          "ja": "jestem",
          "ty": "jesteś",
          "on": "jest",
          "my": "jesteśmy",
          "wy": "jesteście",
          "oni": "są"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l02-c-t02",
      "before": "kpk1-l02-c-e10",
      "title": {
        "en": "He, she, it and they"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "*On* is he, *ona* she and *ono* it, for a child or a neuter noun. In the plural *oni* is for a group with at least one man in it, and *one* for any other group: women, children or things. Formal \"you\" to several people is *panowie* (men), *panie* (women) or *państwo* (men and women), and takes *są*: *gdzie są państwo?*"
      },
      "table": {
        "title": {
          "en": "Pan, pani, państwo"
        },
        "columns": [
          {
            "header": "kto?"
          },
          {
            "header": "oficjalnie"
          }
        ],
